.TH SENSOR-BME680 1 "January 2026" "sensor-bme680 2.0.0" "WildlifeSystems"
.SH NAME
sensor-bme680 \- read BME680 environmental sensor data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sensor-bme680
[\fB\-\-version\fR|\fB\-v\fR|\fBversion\fR|\fBidentify\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBsetup\fR|\fBenable\fR|\fBmock\fR|\fBinternal\fR|\fBexternal\fR|\fBall\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sensor-bme680
reads temperature, humidity, pressure, and gas resistance data from a
Bosch BME680 environmental sensor connected via I2C and outputs the
readings in JSON format.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-v, version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B identify
Exit with code 60 for sensor identification.
.TP
.B list
List available sensor types (temperature, humidity, pressure, gas).
.TP
.B setup
Perform any sensor-specific setup. For BME680, no additional setup is required.
.TP
.B enable
Enable any required kernel interfaces. For BME680, I2C should be enabled
via raspi-config.
.TP
.B mock
Output mock sensor data for testing without hardware. Returns fixed values
(23.5\[de]C temperature, 45% humidity, 1013.25 hPa pressure, 50000 Ohms gas resistance)
useful for testing data pipelines.
.TP
.B internal
Output only readings from sensors marked as internal.
.TP
.B external
Output only readings from sensors marked as external.
.TP
.B all
Output all sensor readings (default if no command given).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ws/sensors/bme680.json
Configuration file for sensor settings.
.SH AUTHOR
Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR i2cdetect (8)
